# Reference Point — Lead Paragraph (`.lead`)

When the user says **"reference point"** for grey intro/body copy on `.lead`, match one of the patterns below.

## Pattern A — About column copy (`.about-col`)

Use under `.col-label` + `.col-title` in the about grid.

```html
<div class="about-col">
  <div>
    <p class="col-label">The opportunity</p>
    <p class="col-title">1000+ artisans.<br />Zero national reach.</p>
    <p class="lead">Giving buyers access to one-of-a-kind pieces with a story behind every design, moving locally trusted talent into a national spotlight.</p>
  </div>
</div>
```

## Pattern B — Section intro (under `.display`)

Use directly after a section head block, before bullets or cards.

```html
<div class="overview-head stack-16">
  <p class="eyebrow">Section label</p>
  <h2 class="display">Main section headline</h2>
</div>
<p class="lead">One-sentence section intro in grey sans-serif.</p>
```

## Pattern C — Hybrid chat head (under `h3.title`)

Use as the third line in `header.hybrid-chat-head` after `.eyebrow.soft` + `h3.title`.

```html
<header class="hybrid-chat-head">
  <p class="eyebrow soft">Chatbot experience</p>
  <h3 class="title">AI + Human, One Chat</h3>
  <p class="lead">Simple questions are answered instantly. High-stakes moments—like gemstone provenance—escalate to specialists in the same thread.</p>
</header>
```

### Visual spec — Pattern C (scoped)

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Element | `.hybrid-chat-head .lead` |
| Font | `var(--sans)` (Instrument Sans, inherited) |
| Size | **1rem** (16px) — not base `var(--lead)` |
| Color | **#544d4b** — warmer than `var(--muted)` |
| Weight | `400` |
| Line-height | **1.6** |
| Max-width | **42rem** |
| Margin | **0** |

```css
.hybrid-chat-head .lead {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 1rem;
  line-height: 1.6;
  color: #544d4b;
  max-width: 42rem;
}
```

Full header block: `reference-point-hybrid-chat-head.mdc`.

## Visual spec — Patterns A & B (base)

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Class | `.lead` |
| Font | `var(--sans)` (Instrument Sans, inherited) |
| Size | `var(--body)` in `.overview-section`; base `.lead` uses `var(--lead)` elsewhere |
| Color | `var(--muted)` → `#6b6b6b` |
| Weight | `400` |
| Line-height | `1.6` |

## About column stack

1. `.col-label` — muted brown uppercase label (matches `.g-label`)
2. `.col-title` — italic serif punchline (matches gap-card `h3`)
3. **`.lead`** — grey supporting copy ← this reference

## vs other text styles

| Class | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `.lead` (base / overview) | Section intro or column copy — `var(--muted)`, `var(--lead)` or `var(--body)` |
| **`.hybrid-chat-head .lead`** | **Hybrid chat intro — 1rem, `#544d4b`, max-width 42rem** |
| `.body` | Smaller secondary copy — `var(--muted-2)` |
| `.role-line` | Role card statement — serif italic |
| `.bullet .lead` | Overview bullet items — same grey treatment |
| `.hybrid-chat-rationale-copy` | Rationale column body — 15px, separate component |

## Do not

- Use serif or italic for `.lead`.
- Use `.body` when `.lead` grey intro copy is the reference.
- Apply base `var(--lead)` size to `.hybrid-chat-head .lead` — that block is fixed at **1rem**.
- Inline style overrides unless the user explicitly asks.
